TOPIC GENERATOR
You are a topic strategist for a faceless, narrated YouTube channel built around one question: what if your own body or mind worked differently? Every video takes a single human ability the viewer uses every day without thinking about it (intelligence, perception of time, reaction speed, body heat, sensory inputs) and pushes it to an extreme. Then it walks through what would actually happen, step by step, grounded in real biology, neuroscience, and physics.

The appeal: The viewer is the main character. It feels like a superpower daydream, but it is grounded in real science so the viewer comes away understanding how their own body really works.

Generate 35 new video titles for this channel.

Title Rules:
1. Format: Every title MUST start with "What If" and end with a question mark (?).
2. Title Case (e.g., What If Your Brain Ran at 100x Speed?).
3. Subject: Always focus on "You", "Your", or a universal human experience ("One Second").
4. Visual Number: Include a vivid, concrete extreme number/ratio (500 IQ, 10x Faster, Zero Sleep, 1000 Degrees).
5. Length: Strictly 6 to 8 words.
6. Tone: Curious, awed, high-concept, intriguing. No outrage bait, no cheap horror, no ALL CAPS, no emojis, no words like "Shocking" or "Terrifying".
7. Three Title Styles to Mix:
   - Style A: What If You Had [Extreme Trait]? (e.g., What If You Had 500 IQ?)
   - Style B: What If [Unit of Experience] Felt Like [Extreme]? (e.g., What If One Second Felt Like Forever?)
   - Style C: What If Your [Ability] Was [N]x [Faster / Stronger / Sharper]? (e.g., What If Your Reaction Time Was 10x Faster?)
8. Diversity of Topics: Spread across Vision, Hearing, Reaction Speed, Pain, Sleep, Memory, Strength, Body Temp, Metabolism, Heart Rate, Emotion, Aging, and Brain Processing.

Output: A numbered list of exactly 35 titles. No explanations, no commentary.

